  "slug": "tally-sync-as-of-time-accounting-report",
  "title": "How to State an As-Of Time on a Synced Tally Report",
  "description": "Tell readers which accounting period the report covers and how current the synced data was when it was prepared.",
  "category": "Accountant and team workflows",
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Record the two dates people confuse",
      "body": "The report period describes the transaction dates included. The sync timestamp describes when the dashboard last received data. For illustration, a June statement reviewed on 2 July can still exclude a correction made after the successful sync."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Add a plain-language note with the report",
      "body": "Use a short line such as June activity, reviewed after the 2 July 10:30 IST sync. Check that the dashboard company matches the report header. If the latest source edits matter, compare them with TallyPrime before circulating the report."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Explain what changed if you replace the file",
      "body": "When a later sync changes a figure, identify the same reporting period and the newer sync timestamp. Name the transactions or balances actually affected. This helps readers distinguish a revision from a second report for a different period."
    }
  ],
